e you hesitate for a  few seconds gazing fearfully waiting for  it to say  it's just me doc i got you pretty good  didn't i and as far as he knows yes he  did you're sure to never slip into the  body language of comfort it's utterly  vital that scp-2006 truly believes that  he's scary to you even though he looks  like a terrible monster costume from an  even worse low-budget b-movie though  specifically the roman the monster from  the 1950 trash classic robot monster you  tell scp 2006 that you're here with some  more stimulus material for him and hand  him a plastic bag when he asks you what  you've brought him this time you tell  him you can't even look at it if you so  much has laid eyes on it you'd slip into  a terrified state of catatonia you'd  honestly rather look at 096 than look at  what you've brought him today scp 2006  cocked his head to the side and asked  what's 096 oh  no  the terror that was fake before wasn't  quite so fake now you'd slipped up buddy  and if you didn't come up with a good  save quickly you would be in deep  trouble you gulp and take a quick breath  trying to compose yourself before saying  that 096 is just another movie one  that's not nearly as scary as the one  you've prepared for him it seemed to  satisfy him so you internally breathe a  sigh of relief and turn to make your  exit you've just left  scp-2006 with a dvd copy of the 1977  classic deathbed the bed that eats a  somewhat obscure horror movie about an  evil bed created by a demon that should  tie the eccentric anomaly over for  another month so you're probably  wondering what actually just happened  what's the logic what are the  connections between the strange sequence  of events we all just witnessed well it  may seem bizarre now once you know more  about  scp-2006 it'll all make sense we can't  promise it'll actually seem any less  bizarre by the end though  scp-2006 is a ketter-class  shape-shifting anomaly its default form  is a floating sphere of about 50  centimeters in diameter not exactly  terrifying and this is actually a big  problem for scp-2000  as the mischievous anomaly has an almost  compulsive desire to scare people not to  physically harm them in any way just  give them a good old-fashioned spook  he's shown to be pretty much  indestructible so neutralization is off  the table you may be thinking he seems  like a pretty harmless goofball why  would anyone want to neutralize him and  well we'll answer that one later back to  scp-2006's favorite hobby scaring people  while 2006 seems to practically live off  of giving a good scare he's thankfully  no pennywise 2006 has no inherent  knowledge of what scares humans and thus  has to learn what scares humans from  external sources this unique weakness to  scp-2006's ability is one the foundation  has discovered as an ingenious method of  exploiting for its containment they  simply keep  scp-2006 misinformed on what people  actually find scary tricking it to make  sure that it's always hopelessly inept  at its hobby their method of achieving  this is twofold firstly they give  scp-2006 a monthly supply of the worst  horror movies you can imagine true  bargain bucket b-movie schlock troll 2  leprechaun in the hood birdemic shock  and terror a personal favorite the  ginger dead man the beast of yucca flats  plan 9 from outer space a runner-up for  me the creeping terror the man without a  body manos the hands of fate track of  the moon beast and of course the seminal  classic iga a movie about an evil  caveman being unfrozen and  terrorizing palm springs movies like  this are a perfect mechanism for  tricking scp-2006  because it sees the characters in the  movies reacting with fear to the  terrible hokey monsters rampaging across  backlots and sound stages and starts to  believe that these b-movie beasts are  actually scary that's the first part of  the trick and you've probably already  figured out the second half the  foundation makes sure that any employees  who interact with scp 2006 in any  capacity must play the part of appearing  actually genuinely frightened by it this  one-two punch of trickery keeps scp-2006  successfully bamboozled as such despite  being a creature largely based around  creating fear albeit in a more friendly  playful way than most anomalies it's  seen as a joke among staff members it  wouldn't be surprising to hear that  different staff members took turns  laughing at surveillance footage or that  the latest site halloween party a few  drunken researchers tried to trick  scp-2006 into assuming the form of david  s pumpkins from saturday night live i  believe they also received angry phone  calls from tom hanks's agent the next  day as you could probably gather  developing such an unimpressed attitude  to containing anomalies with the scp  foundation is never a good thing after  all even some of the most innocent  looking ones can hide surprisingly dark  secrets dr randall owings the site  director for site 118 where scp-2006 is  held released a stern memorandum to  everyone working in 2006's proximity it  read i've been getting reports of some  of the lacks behavior regarding scp-2006  many personnel have been heard laughing  at scp-2006 during surveillance when it  watches a new movie or when it attempts  to scare individuals some personnel have  been heard questioning why scp-2006 is  classified as a ketter entity i am here  to remind you that a ketter entity is a  ketter entity regardless of how  innocuous it may seem no scp-2006  is not a rampaging demigod nor is it a  regenerating super lizard however it  possesses the same level of danger as  any other ketter that the foundation has  contained think of scp-2006 scp-2006's  purpose it wishes to scare people  imagine what would happen if scp-2006  broke containment and found out what  really scared people imagine if it saw  the horror and fear of war or the  concepts of paranoia or phobia is common  to each and every human being imagine if  it found 